      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to consider the time and speed at which the train is moving and the length of the tunnel/track.\n\n1. First, we convert the train speed from miles per hour to miles per minute:\n\n$$60 \\text{ miles per hour} = 60 \\text{ miles} \\div 60 \\text{ minutes}$$\n\nSince there are 120 minutes in 60 hours (60*60), we have:\n\n$$60 \\text{ miles per hour} = \\frac{60}{120} \\text{ miles per minute}$$\n\n2. We compute the distance the train travels in 3 minutes:\n\n(Train speed / Time) = 60 / 120 = 0.5 miles\n\nThis indicates that the train has traveled 0.5 miles in the 3 minutes before exiting the tunnel.\n\n3. Now, consider the length of the tunnel:\n\nThe distance the train traveled in 3 minutes is the sum of the distance the train would have traveled without the tunnel and the length of the tunnel:\n\nLength of tunnel + 0.5 miles = 1 mile\n\nSolving for the length of the tunnel:\n\n(Length of tunnel) = 1 mile - 0.5 miles\n(Length of tunnel) = 0.5 miles\n\nHence, the answer is:\n\n\\boxed{0.5}",
